# Everything listed here stays OUT of the build context. Two reasons: a
# smaller, faster build, and — more importantly — no secret can be COPYed
# into a published layer by a future Dockerfile edit.
#
# The image only needs: cpanfile, lib/, web/ (sources for the Vite build).

# Git
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# IDE
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo

# Node modules (the build installs fresh ones)
node_modules/
web/node_modules
**/node_modules

# Data directories
data/
logs/
*.log

# Tests / e2e — never shipped in the image
t/
tests/
web/e2e/
coverage/

# Documentation
*.md
!README.md
docs/

# CREDENTIALS.md holds real secrets. The *.md glob above already catches it,
# but only by coincidence — a single `!*.md` would put it in the context.
# Keep this line explicit.
CREDENTIALS.md

# Local config and env files. ALL variants, not just `.env` / `.env.local`:
# .env.production, .env.dev, .env.local.bak have exactly the same blast
# radius as .env.
.env
.env.*
config/
config/local.yaml
.credentials

# Infra / deploy manifests — not part of the runtime image
chart/
deploy/
install.sh
docker-compose*.yml
Makefile

# Planning / agent state
.planning/
.beads/
.claude/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
